(4583565, 657235, 22970, '<td valign="top">Amazing- What an awesome scene. I didn''t get to vote on the complete challenge because of personal obligations but I wish I would had been able to. This would of received another 10. Very impressed with the B&amp;W process, so much detail and range. This has to go into my fav''s.<br/>Very nice work. IMO probably one of the best B&amp;W photos I have viewed to date.<br/>Congrats<br/></td>', 'Amazing- What an awesome scene. I didn''t get to vote on the complete challenge because of personal obligations but I wish I would had been able to. This would of received another 10. Very impressed with the B&W process, so much detail and range. This has to go into my fav''s.Very nice work. IMO probably one of the best B&W photos I have viewed to date.Congrats', '2008-03-24 14:38:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4583575, 658631, 51538, '<td valign="top">À Paris c''est votre magnétisme, Monsieur, elle ne pourrait pas vous résister.</td>', 'À Paris c''est votre magnétisme, Monsieur, elle ne pourrait pas vous résister.', '2008-03-24 14:43:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4583598, 658763, 84452, '<td valign="top">Where were you when you took this? While I spend most of the year in central Florida, I have a home in Berrien County, MI. I''ve take a lot of pictures in both Michigan City as well as of the St. Joe lighthouse. I might have guessed you were standing  on the MC lighthouse walkway, looking towards Chicago in the late afternoon. But the land on the far left horizon suggests it was someplace else.  I don''t think I''ve ever seen Lake Michigan colored as it was the day you took the picture. Nice work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-24 14:56:48.</i></td>', 'Where were you when you took this? While I spend most of the year in central Florida, I have a home in Berrien County, MI. I''ve take a lot of pictures in both Michigan City as well as of the St. Joe lighthouse. I might have guessed you were standing  on the MC lighthouse walkway, looking towards Chicago in the late afternoon. But the land on the far left horizon suggests it was someplace else.  I don''t think I''ve ever seen Lake Michigan colored as it was the day you took the picture. Nice work.', '2008-03-24 14:55:41.000000', '2008-03-24 14:56:48.000000', 0),
