(4583825, 658763, 42495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by VillagesKahuna:</b></div><hr/><i> Where were you when you took this? While I spend most of the year in central Florida, I have a home in Berrien County, MI. I''ve take a lot of pictures in both Michigan City as well as of the St. Joe lighthouse. I might have guessed you were standing  on the MC lighthouse walkway, looking towards Chicago in the late afternoon. But the land on the far left horizon suggests it was someplace else.  I don''t think I''ve ever seen Lake Michigan colored as it was the day you took the picture. Nice work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are correct - it was taken from the walkway looking just a bit South of Chicago.  It''s hard to see but the land on the left is mostly dunes.</td>', 'Originally posted by VillagesKahuna: Where were you when you took this? While I spend most of the year in central Florida, I have a home in Berrien County, MI. I''ve take a lot of pictures in both Michigan City as well as of the St. Joe lighthouse. I might have guessed you were standing  on the MC lighthouse walkway, looking towards Chicago in the late afternoon. But the land on the far left horizon suggests it was someplace else.  I don''t think I''ve ever seen Lake Michigan colored as it was the day you took the picture. Nice work.   You are correct - it was taken from the walkway looking just a bit South of Chicago.  It''s hard to see but the land on the left is mostly dunes.', '2008-03-24 17:01:38.000000', NULL, 0),
