(4590052, 657388, 39638, '<td valign="top">this was a totally sarcastic title that I put on there... there is this dog who actually turns out to be a female-- don''t know who she belongs to.. and she had pups and no one can find them.. and people drive by our front yard going 80 mph  (really)<br/>so i walk around and take pics and she quietly follows and never makes a peep-- I really like taking pics -- but I am not so big on -- nor do I understand the whole iso shutter -- aperature thing very much .. i have read my manual when I have a buzz... so I don''t remember what it was that I read...ha</td>', 'this was a totally sarcastic title that I put on there... there is this dog who actually turns out to be a female-- don''t know who she belongs to.. and she had pups and no one can find them.. and people drive by our front yard going 80 mph  (really)so i walk around and take pics and she quietly follows and never makes a peep-- I really like taking pics -- but I am not so big on -- nor do I understand the whole iso shutter -- aperature thing very much .. i have read my manual when I have a buzz... so I don''t remember what it was that I read...ha', '2008-03-26 21:52:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4591113, 658548, 15291, '<td valign="top">First let me say WOW !, simply magnificent.<br/> <br/><b>The Title/Challenge</b> <br/> <br/>I like the title of the capture it fits well with the challenge giving us the best of both worlds paradise &amp; harsh, nice mix.<br/> <br/><b>The Border</b> <br/> <br/>The border is nicely done, the green &amp; black work well together here giving a nice accent to the image. I see way to many borders that are over done and a distraction. This was done just right.<br/> <br/><b>The background</b> <br/> <br/>Very nice use of DFO here we get just enough to recognize the glades without being a distraction or detracting from your focal point. Well done.<br/> <br/><b>The composition</b> <br/> <br/>What can I say outstanding.<br/> <br/><b>The tonality</b> <br/> <br/>Very well done the colors are deep and have lots of pop.<br/> <br/><b>Over all</b> <br/> <br/>Just a great image all the way around the image has interest, eye popping color, nice clean, crisp focus. The details in the Heron &amp; frog are fantastic, and an awesome composition. Well done !!<br/></td>', 'First let me say WOW !, simply magnificent. The Title/Challenge  I like the title of the capture it fits well with the challenge giving us the best of both worlds paradise & harsh, nice mix. The Border  The border is nicely done, the green & black work well together here giving a nice accent to the image. I see way to many borders that are over done and a distraction. This was done just right. The background  Very nice use of DFO here we get just enough to recognize the glades without being a distraction or detracting from your focal point. Well done. The composition  What can I say outstanding. The tonality  Very well done the colors are deep and have lots of pop. Over all  Just a great image all the way around the image has interest, eye popping color, nice clean, crisp focus. The details in the Heron & frog are fantastic, and an awesome composition. Well done !!', '2008-03-27 10:45:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4591142, 658457, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi,<br/> A very nice effort, and nice image. There are a few things here that need to be addressed that you may find helpful.<br/> <br/>The first thing that jumped out at me was the amount of noise in the image. I see you set your ISO at 50. I am not firmiliar with you camera but shooting this at ISO 200 may have worked better for you here. Most all of the cameras today vary in there noise levels the higher or lower you go with the ISO the more or less nosie.<br/> <br/> Second there seems to be something on your lense (right side center of the image) there seems to be dust or something.<br/> <br/> Thirdly with the cloud cover being so deep with the defused lighting waiting around a bit may have affored you the opportunity of some dramatic lighting. As it was you took your image directly into the sun causeing it to be a bit of a distraction and slightly hot. Next time this opportunity comes along try a higher ISO, wait for the sun to rise a bit more &amp; stay awhile, dramatic lighting usually arise from these situations making for some stunning images. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi, A very nice effort, and nice image. There are a few things here that need to be addressed that you may find helpful. The first thing that jumped out at me was the amount of noise in the image. I see you set your ISO at 50. I am not firmiliar with you camera but shooting this at ISO 200 may have worked better for you here. Most all of the cameras today vary in there noise levels the higher or lower you go with the ISO the more or less nosie.  Second there seems to be something on your lense (right side center of the image) there seems to be dust or something.  Thirdly with the cloud cover being so deep with the defused lighting waiting around a bit may have affored you the opportunity of some dramatic lighting. As it was you took your image directly into the sun causeing it to be a bit of a distraction and slightly hot. Next time this opportunity comes along try a higher ISO, wait for the sun to rise a bit more & stay awhile, dramatic lighting usually arise from these situations making for some stunning images.  ', '2008-03-27 11:20:02.000000', NULL, 0),
